Sail: a "Page style" card in the Customize panel (the pencil on the New Tab
page): shortcut size, frosted glass behind the icons, shortcut names, a clock
with a greeting, and how dark and blurred the wallpaper is. In a shortcut's
Edit dialog you can also give it your own icon. Both are stored as JSON in
two profile prefs (chrome/browser/ui/sail/sail_ntp_prefs.h), which the
browser only passes between the panel and the page.

Shortcuts also show the large icon their site declares (apple-touch-icon,
or the largest icon of 96 px or more; Google's product icons for its apps)
instead of a blown-up favicon. The browser reads the page without cookies to
find it, chrome://image downloads and decodes it in a sandboxed process, and
the page remembers the result for a week.

The shortcuts' hover lifts the icon instead of lighting up the tile, their
menu button sits on the icon's corner and shows at once, and the Edit /
Remove menu and the add / edit dialog (with the icon on top, like editing
an app) are restyled.

